# Hope for All Foundation — Community Upliftment Web Platform (Part 3)

## Project Information
- **Repository Link:** https://github.com/nevhutaludakalodk-web/Dakalo-part-2[span_3]
- **Live Deployed Site:** https://nevhutaludakalodk-web.github.io/Dakalo-part-2/

## Part 3 Enhancement Overview
- **JavaScript Enhancements:** Leaflet.js interactive mapping, live client-side search filtering, dynamic lightbox gallery modal, smooth back-to-top navigation, and collapsible accordions.
- **Form Validation & Processing:**
  - `enquiry.html`: Validates South African phone number formats and dynamically computes availability, volunteer orientation schedules, or sponsorship costing outputs.
  - `contact.html`: Validates inputs and compiles a formatted `mailto` trigger for direct email transmission.
- **SEO Optimization:** Includes `<meta name="description">` and `<meta name="keywords">` across all headers, structured `H1`-`H3` tags, descriptive image `alt` tags, `robots.txt`, and `sitemap.xml`.

## Complete Changelog

### Version 3.0.0 (Part 3 Release)
- **Part 2 Feedback Amendments:** Standardized CSS styling, verified link integrity, and ensured comprehensive image alt-text across all cards.
- **SEO Setup:** Configured `robots.txt` and `sitemap.xml` at the root directory. Added page-specific meta descriptions and keywords.
- **Interactive Mapping:** Replaced static map iframe on `contact.html` with an interactive OpenStreetMap powered by Leaflet.js.
- **Lightbox Feature:** Implemented responsive full-screen image preview modal in `js/main.js`.
- **Live Search Filter:** Built search bar functionality filtering menu and event items in real time.
- **Form Processing Engine:** Integrated client-side regex phone validation and dynamic response output cards in `js/enquiry.js` and `js/contact.js`.

